            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in angina management: implications for nurses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-56; quiz 58</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the physiology of the heart and the pathophysiology of angina. Diagnosis and treatment options, including pharmacological therapies, are outlined. The authors also discuss cardiac rehabilitation programmes and the extended role of nurses in managing patients with angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
